/*\n
|--------------------------------------------------------------------------\n
| PROMPT 5: public National Lottery result surface\n
|--------------------------------------------------------------------------\n
|\n
| A SEPARATE PRODUCT LANE. These four routes serve national_lottery_* data and\n
| nothing else: not GLO L6/N3, not an operator market, not a lottery provider\n
| that has not published. They read; nothing here writes.\n
|\n
| ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING. /search, /buy, /latest, /history, /year/{year},\n
| /archive/{year}, /draw/{draw} and /result/{draw} are declared BEFORE /{draw}.\n
| Reversed, the wildcard would capture a literal page segment and turn it into\n
| a draw lookup.\n
|\n
| PARAMETER PATTERNS ARE HARD BOUNDARIES. {year} is at most four decimal\n
| digits and {draw} is at most forty characters of an explicit alphabet, so a\n
| hostile URL is refused by the router before a controller, a validator or a\n
| query is ever reached.\n
|\n
| /search carries throttle:national-result-search (registered in\n
| AppServiceProvider from config('national_lottery.rate_limit')): IP per\n
| minute, IP per hour, and a hashed query fingerprint per minute. robots.txt\n
| asks crawlers to stay out of the same path, but that is a request - this\n
| limiter is the control.\n
|\n
| public.legal = PublicLegalHeaders: short guest-GET cache headers on the\n
| listed cacheable paths only. The search route is deliberately outside that\n
| list, so a query-dependent response is never cached at the edge.\n
*/\n
